1 NOTE Luigi (Alviso, or Louis) Almoro Du Pisani was born in Venice, Italy, sometime before 1767, the son of Alviso Almoro Pisany and Caroline Joan Elizabeth Coxner. He joined the Dutch East India Company in 1780 and was at the Cape by 1
2 CONC 781 - the first Italian immigrant to the Cape.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1783 he found himself in the Camdeboo where he took part in the unsuccesful Muller-Holtzhausen expedition, sent to look for survivors of the wreck of the Grosvenor. He went AWOL to Ceylon, but is back in Graaff-Reinet by 1786.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT By 1788 he is again in the service of the Dutch East India Company as a sailor. In 1792 he becomes a farmer, and in 1795 he is given the farm Brakkefontein. In July of that year he joined the Swellendam rebellion and helps to draf
2 CONC t the manifesto of a National Assembly. As commander of a group of 22 soldiers of the assembly he terrorizes the countryside and threatens to burn down the Baviaanskloof mission (later known as Genadendal). He is declared an outla
2 CONC w by Governer Sluysken, who puts a large price on his head. His followers leave him and in August of 1795 he is arrested by a Captain Bresler with the assistance of citizens, and imprisoned in the castle at Cape Town. He is exiled
2 CONC  to the Netherlands, where he commits some or other crime, and runs off to France. In 1798 his wife in the Cape, Dinah Joan Crafford, divorces him. Their eldest son, Louis Almoro, retains the family name, and later becomes a publi
2 CONC can in the Swellendam area.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT A family legend has it that Alviso's father was the owner of the Villa Pisani on the river Brenta, and doge of Venice from 1735 to 1740. According to this legend, Alviso was to inherit the family properties, but after a pistol due
2 CONC l with his younger brother ran off to join the French Army, where he added the "Du" in front of his name. For some reason, and in contradiction of both history and legend, my mother's family considered themselves French Hugenots.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis Almero Du Pisani has remained a family name. I have two cousins with the full family name, and my brother is called Almero.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bron: Gideon Strauss: http://www.gideonstrauss.com/archive/2003_08_31_archive.html
