1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Count Alvise Francesco Mocenigo was a Venetian nobleman who served in all three roles (spettacoli, cassiere, economia) within the Presidente of the Teatro la Fenice in Venice. Mocenigo first met Giuseppe Verdi in 1
2 CONC 842 in Vienna at the revival of Nabucco and mounted Venetian productions of I Lombardi in 1843. He commisioned Ernani for 1844, actively participating in the choice of subject and genesis of the libretto, recommending that Verdi c
2 CONC ollaborate with Francesco Maria Piave on the text, and overseeing the opera's premiere. Verdi dedicated the piano-vocal score of Ernani to Mocenigo's (first) wife, Countess Clementina Spaun. (Source: The Cambridge Verdi Encycloped
2 CONC ia, pages 287-288)
