1 NAME Jacob Naude /Smith/
2 GIVN Jacob Naude
2 _MARNM Smith
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 19 JUL 1911
2 ADDR
3 CITY Brandfort
3 STAE Free State
3 CTRY South Africa
1 DEAT
2 DATE 15 MAY 1948
2 PLAC Roxdale Farm Spitzkop Mountain
2 ADDR
3 CITY Vrede
3 STAE OFS
3 CTRY South Africa
1 OCCU Pilot
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} - Jacob won a Gold medal for SA ( boxing flyweight) at the first ever Commonwealth Empire games in Canada in 1930. During the WW2 , Jacob was awarded the Distinguished Flying Cross. (31SQN). Jacob was one of the pi
2 CONC lots in one of the first commercial airline crashes in South Africa in 1947
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born July 19, 1911 in Brandfort, Free State. His parents were Matthys Gerhardus Smith and Elizabeth Catharina Smith (Naude). Jacob's brother was the well known Afrikaans author of the Trompie and Saartjie children's books .
2 CONC ... Mathys Gerhardus Smith (Topsy). In 1930 Jacob represented South Africa at Commonwealth Empire games in Canada. The 18 year old flyweight who the previous year had boxed as a junior, caused one of the biggest upsets when he sco
2 CONC red a narrow points decision over Tim Pardoe of England in the final to win a gold medal. He was also known as "Babe Smith" in the boxing world. He was experienced, too, in bad-weather flying - he had recently flown from London to
2 CONC  Athens entirely in cloud at 1 000 feet. On 15 May 1948 Jacob, on his way to Palmietfontein airport, crashed his Douglas DC-3-455 (registration ZS-BWY) into the Spitzkop mountain near Memel in the OFS. There were 13 fatalities inc
2 CONC luding his wife Maria Elizabeth Smith (Mitchel). Jacob and Maria left behind 5 children all under the age of 13. All five children have since passed away before their time from a variety of ailments.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Any information on any of the abovementioned will be appreciated, particularly photo's from his flying days during and after the war http://www.dc-3.co.za/dc-3-south-african-operators/mercury-airways.html
2 CONT
2 CONT Death Notice: https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3Q9M-CS3Q-4ST7-T?lang=en&i=1097&cc=2520237
