1 NOTE {geni:about_me} John Viljoen apparently lived in Kaffir River (renamed Tierpoort) near Bloemfontein. He was briefly married to my paternal Grandmother Florance Hobbs. Floss told my dad that his dad (John) had died in the war. Kids
2 CONC  at his primary school put him right and he went home and asked his gran if it was true. She then said that he was not a very nice man and had left. She never spoke about it again and went to her grave with the secret. My dad rece
2 CONC ived a visit from his grandfather at school once and also got a letter with R500 in, informing him that his dad had died in 1968.  Floss changed both her and my dad's names back to her maiden name, Hobbs.
